      "writtenOn": "2017-10-18T19:29:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "suppose that the input lists are:\n\n[\"B\",\"C\"], [\"A\",\"B\"]\n\nwhere A has surprisingly not declared a transitive dependency on C.\n\nThen the concatenation is [\"B\",\"C\",\"A\",\"B\"]\nand the last unique elements is [\"C\", \"A\", \"B\"]\n\n\nDo you think I should rename the variables from [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"] to [\"B\", \"C\", \"D\"] to clarify that triggering this case requires four modules in total?\n\nSee also https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/496454/4/cc/cc_test.go#398\n\nAlso, do you think that this behavior in this case is correct?",
      "parentUuid": "bf12c1e7_43945682",
      "revId": "d4f0f3081f4a19fab2d9f845bfb667975735af28",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "683968bb_288e3d4e",
